Sorry if this is the second report of this problem, but even so,
there is some more information.
The problem is that when I run the completely compiled nethack game
on my Apollo DN3500 under SR10.1/BSD4.3, with the TERM and TERMCAP
variables set properly, along with HACKOPTIONS, the program doesn't
send any terminal control characters -- the program runs completely
right, and doesn't give any errors, but it's as if the "tgoto()", etc,
calls are returning null strings.  Thus, the entire game is printed
all on one line.
At first I thought I had caught the cause of the problem -- I had
the linking options as "-ltermlib" instead of "-ltermcap", but even
after changing that, the program ran the same.

I have a suspicion that it is not obtaining the environment variables --
the HACKOPTIONS don't show up quite right..  But even so, it would seem
that it would still send conrtol characters.  Just as I said above,
it's as if the term routines are returning nulls.

An by the way, I did set up the #define APOLLO, whatever that does.

Thanks for any suggestions -- it's very frustrating to be able to
play the game but not be able to see it!
